      section: "CS",
      q: "A regular language L is accepted by a non-deterministic finite automaton (NFA) with n states. Which of the following statement(s) is/are FALSE? (A) L may have an accepting NFA with < n states. (B) L may have an accepting DFA with < n states. (C) There exists a DFA with ≤ 2^n states that accepts L. (D) Every DFA that accepts L has > 2^n states.",
      options: ["L may have an accepting NFA with < n states.","L may have an accepting DFA with < n states.","There exists a DFA with ≤ 2^n states that accepts L.","Every DFA that accepts L has > 2^n states."],
      answers: [3],
