      q: "A = {0, 1, 2, 3, ...} is the set of non-negative integers. Let F be the set of functions from A to itself. For any two functions f1, f2 ∈ F, we define (f1 ⊙ f2)(n) = f1(n) + f2(n) for every number n in A. Which of the following is/are CORRECT about the mathematical structure (F, ⊙)?",
